cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "hills: frozen evaluations for unattended agent optimization loops"
message: "If you use hills in your work, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Artem
    family-names: Lukoianov
    affiliation: Autolab
  - given-names: Serge
    family-names: Klein
    affiliation: Autolab
  - given-names: Serge
    family-names: Didenko
    affiliation: Autolab
repository-code: "https://github.com/autolab-ai/hills"
url: "https://github.com/autolab-ai/hills"
abstract: >-
  hills packages an evaluation into a frozen, versioned directory so that an
  agent can run an optimization loop unattended without grading its own work.
  The agent develops freely, but a score exists only if the frozen evaluator
  produced it, and every score comes back signed and tied to the exact version
  of the evaluation that produced it.
keywords:
  - evaluation
  - benchmark
  - agents
  - verification
  - machine-learning
